#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186354646 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157437 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3758cf02-ba4b-539a-bc61-8c2030ff6f6f" :knowledge-point/title "Solving an Exponential Equation by Factoring"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "33737a4b-5342-5565-914a-cb6438076b5b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186352043} {:answer/id #uuid "380810d5-4536-54a8-96a6-03ca61571cf7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186352085} {:answer/id #uuid "4d84059a-bf3e-5ad8-848d-de47fb5fcbba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186352275} {:answer/id #uuid "8597e99b-a624-5fb1-9f86-e86812b0613d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186352731} {:answer/id #uuid "da180e83-5bee-502b-9c12-ae8aed810433" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353461}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "da180e83-5bee-502b-9c12-ae8aed810433" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353461} :answer-field/id #uuid "15a5b309-fce0-58d4-9cb6-f4a8f8750bae" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353852}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "395668d0-2b32-5884-a30f-d67a196224fd" :question/math-academy-id "q-88460" :question/problem "What is the product of solutions of the equation $2{x}^{2}\\cdot {6}^{x+3}-9x\\cdot {6}^{x+3}+4\\cdot {6}^{x+3}=0?$" :question/worked-solution "First, we factor the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{x}^{2}\\cdot {6}^{x+3}-9x\\cdot {6}^{x+3}+4\\cdot {6}^{x+3} & =0 \\\\ (2{x}^{2}-9x+4){6}^{x+3} & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now apply the zero product property, which states that $ab=0$ if and only if $a=0$ or $b=0.$ This gives us two equations,\n\n$$\n2{x}^{2}-9x+4=0\\,\\text{and}\\,{6}^{x+3}=0.\n$$\n\nWe now solve each of these equations separately.\n\n- The equation $2{x}^{2}-9x+4=0$ can be factored as\n\n$$\n(2x-1)(x-4)=0,\n$$\n\nwhich leads to the solutions $x=\\frac{1}{2},4.$\n\n- The equation ${6}^{x+3}=0$ has no solutions because ${6}^{x+3}$ is positive for every real number $x.$\n\nTherefore, the original equation has the solutions $x=\\frac{1}{2},4,$ and their product is $\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 4=2.$"}]}
